OL,3,GNEWSA'I won't let life-changing crash
OL,4,Adefine me,' says 20-year-old
OL,5,
OL,6,FA young man who suffered life-changing
OL,7,Fbrain and spinal injuries in a crash
OL,8,Fhas said he does not want to be
OL,9,F"defined" by the incident.
OL,11,FJoshua Kay-Shaw, from Ripon, also
OL,12,Fsuffered fractured ribs, a fractured
OL,13,Fbreastbone and a punctured lung when
OL,14,Fthe car he was a passenger in collided
OL,15,Fwith another vehicle on Marston Lane in
OL,16,FYork, in December 2023.
OL,18,FThe 20-year-old, who was studying
OL,19,Faccounting at York College at the time,
OL,20,Fspent four months in hospital and now
OL,21,Fuses a wheelchair.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
